WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.250
- Now, you say that achieving good sleep

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.630
starts even before bedtime.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:07.840
Enlighten me.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.050
- So, I always think
about sleep as like an on,

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.360
it's not an on/off switch,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.860
it's more like a dimmer switch.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.950
So doing a wind-down
routine, ideally an hour,

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.490
but most of us don't have an hour.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:21.360
So start with five minutes of relaxation,

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.570
whatever you find is quieting,

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.660
just do it for five minutes,
then move to 10 minutes,

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:27.250
and really try to set that stage.

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.120
And the other thing I also would argue

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.360
is that a good bedtime comes
with a good morning time.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.490
So if you're consistent

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:35.610
with the morning wake up-time every day,

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.030
you get bright light, you move,

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.600
you have a big glass of water,

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.240
that actually helps to set your bedtime

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.238
so you fall asleep a
little bit better as well.

00:00:42.238 --> 00:00:44.821
(bright music)

00:00:46.731 --> 00:00:49.148
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

